From: AsherJN
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: Follow audio devices added, removed and made default while a program runs.

Adapted for CrossOver 26.3 from AsherJN/recall commit a436e4cd4fac44693b4d699acc030d17eec6f36e
(patches/wine-audio-devices.patch). Its policy of using the built-in
microphone while the default one is a Bluetooth headset's is not
carried; the default microphone is the one chosen in macOS. A downstream
fix, not a WineHQ backport.

mmdevapi lists the audio devices once, when it loads. A program never
learns about headphones connected or removed, or a new default device,
while it runs, and keeps using a device that is gone.

winecoreaudio.drv now watches the Core Audio device list and default
devices, and a new unix call, wait_device_change, returns once changes
settle. mmdevapi starts a thread for it with that driver only, lists the
devices again and tells registered IMMNotificationClient objects what
changed, as Windows does: OnDeviceAdded, OnDeviceStateChanged and
OnDefaultDeviceChanged. A lock now guards the device list and the default
devices. Once mmdevapi has listed the devices again, a stream whose
device is gone returns AUDCLNT_E_DEVICE_INVALIDATED from
GetCurrentPadding, Start, GetBuffer and GetNextPacketSize, so a program
that reopens the default device gets the new one; a reconnected device
normally gets a new ID, so the stream stays invalid, as on Windows.
DirectSound and winmm only log these errors and do not reopen the device.
The watch thread runs in every process that loads mmdevapi and pins
mmdevapi and the driver.

The unix call is added to the shared driver function table; only
winecoreaudio.drv implements it, and the other drivers report it as not
implemented. mmdevapi and the driver must come from the same build.

